# Hub notifications (LOCKED global standard)

Ephemeral user feedback across Hub (dApps, Games, Tokens, Store, vBlog, Chronicles, Magazines, Ads, Rewards) uses one system: bottom-right toast cards.

## Source of truth

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Provider UI | `src/components/ui/Toaster.tsx` (`ToasterProvider`, already in `Providers`) |
| Hook + helpers | `useHubNotify()` / `hubNotify` from `@/lib/hub/notify` (also re-exported from `@/hooks/useToast`) |
| Imperative bridge | `src/lib/hub/notifyBridge.ts` (do not call from UI; used by provider) |

## Do this

- On important actions (pay, publish, send, save, vote, refine ack, validation fail that blocks submit): call `useHubNotify()` or `hubNotify.*`.
- Variants: `success` | `error` | `warning` | `info` | `loading`.
- Transactions: show `loading(...)` while signing/broadcasting, then `txSuccess({ title, txHash, chainId? })` or `update(id, …)` so the same card flips. Include explorer link via `txSuccess` (Kaspa L1 default; pass EVM `chainId` for L2).
- Forms / editors: toast for submit errors ("Title is required") and success; do not invent a second popup stack.
- Toasts stay until the user clicks **x** (default `duration: 0` for all variants). Pass a positive `duration` only when a toast should auto-dismiss.
- Keep rail/`Alert` only for **persistent** field help (`KX_INFO_DASHED`, ownership gates, sticky contextual notes). Prefer toast for one-shot action feedback.

## Do not

- Add sonner / react-hot-toast / a second toaster.
- Use `window.alert` for Hub UX.
- Mount another `ToasterProvider` per page or product.
- Leave duplicate success/error banners in calculation rails when a toast already covers the same event.
- Fork toast chrome per dApp/game; change `Toaster.tsx` once for Hub-wide look.

## Quick API

```ts
const n = useHubNotify();
const id = n.loading('Sending…', 'Confirm in wallet');
// …
n.txSuccess({ id, title: 'KREX sent', txHash });
n.error('Missing fields', 'Title and description are required.');
// or: hubNotify.success('Saved');
```
